1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:03,940
It's the last day of Primary 3, and the class party at

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:06,270
the void deck starts in twenty minutes!

3
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:09,167
But the ice cream is still here at the mama shop, and

4
00:00:09,187 --> 00:00:11,136
it's thirty-three degrees outside!

5
00:00:11,258 --> 00:00:13,268
Ice cream against the Singapore sun.

6
00:00:13,428 --> 00:00:14,899
The sun always wins.

7
00:00:15,096 --> 00:00:16,196
Don't worry.

8
00:00:16,386 --> 00:00:17,596
I've got a plan!

9
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:20,076
Actually, I've got three plans!

10
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:20,876
Oh no.

11
00:00:21,227 --> 00:00:22,957
The Great Ice Cream Rescue!

12
00:00:23,534 --> 00:00:25,694
Plan one, I run super fast.

13
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:28,154
Plan two, we fan it all the way.

14
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:31,014
Plan three, I wrap it in my wool scarf!

15
00:00:31,366 --> 00:00:34,556
Which fix gets the ice cream to the party still frozen?

16
00:00:34,837 --> 00:00:36,956
Show me one, two or three fingers!

17
00:00:43,579 --> 00:00:44,299
One!

18
00:00:44,569 --> 00:00:46,069
Speed is my thing!

19
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:46,940
Two!

20
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,770
Wind is nice and cool!

21
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:49,611
Three.

22
00:00:49,721 --> 00:00:50,721
The scarf.

23
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:51,470
Wool?

24
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,260
Wool is warm, Basil!

25
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:54,590
You'll melt it!

26
00:00:54,864 --> 00:00:56,014
Three fixes.

27
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:58,204
Let's test them, one by one!

28
00:00:58,550 --> 00:00:59,500
Fix one.

29
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:00,780
Pip runs!

30
00:01:02,404 --> 00:01:03,254
Phew!

31
00:01:03,474 --> 00:01:07,774
Too far! I'll just hug it close, to keep it warm and safe.

32
00:01:07,861 --> 00:01:08,681
Warm?

33
00:01:08,811 --> 00:01:10,331
Pip, it's ice cream!

34
00:01:10,649 --> 00:01:13,489
Brr! My tummy feels cold!

35
00:01:13,669 --> 00:01:15,859
The cold is going into my tummy!

36
00:01:16,099 --> 00:01:17,259
Not quite, Pip.

37
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:19,219
Nothing cold is flowing.

38
00:01:19,499 --> 00:01:22,949
Your tummy is warmer than the ice cream, so heat flows out

39
00:01:22,969 --> 00:01:24,679
of your tummy into the ice cream.

40
00:01:24,949 --> 00:01:28,859
Your tummy loses heat, and the ice cream gains heat and melts!

41
00:01:31,504 --> 00:01:32,684
Speed, amazing.

42
00:01:32,814 --> 00:01:34,234
Stamina, chinchilla.

43
00:01:34,588 --> 00:01:35,638
Fix two.

44
00:01:35,918 --> 00:01:37,658
Momo fans the ice cream!

45
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:39,107
Fan, fan, fan!

46
00:01:39,197 --> 00:01:41,127
Cool wind for my ice cream!

47
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:42,740
Oh no!

48
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,110
It's dripping!

49
00:01:44,458 --> 00:01:46,961
Let's look at that again, in slow motion.

50
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:48,623
Oh no!

51
00:01:49,405 --> 00:01:51,911
It's dripping!

52
00:01:52,107 --> 00:01:53,257
Look closer.

53
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:55,777
A fan cannot make air cold.

54
00:01:56,357 --> 00:01:58,237
It only pushes the air along.

55
00:01:58,807 --> 00:02:03,107
This air is thirty-three degrees, and the ice cream is about minus

56
00:02:03,127 --> 00:02:04,887
eighteen degrees Celsius.

57
00:02:05,171 --> 00:02:07,811
Heat flows from a hotter place to a colder place.

58
00:02:08,021 --> 00:02:11,381
So heat flows from the warm air into the cold ice cream!

59
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:12,862
Yes!

60
00:02:13,422 --> 00:02:17,022
The fan pushes more warm air past the ice cream, so more

61
00:02:17,042 --> 00:02:19,722
heat flows in, and it melts faster.

62
00:02:22,288 --> 00:02:24,528
So the fan is a heat delivery service.

63
00:02:24,803 --> 00:02:26,863
We only have fifteen minutes left!

64
00:02:26,913 --> 00:02:28,883
This is a snack emergency!

65
00:02:29,081 --> 00:02:30,241
Fix three!

66
00:02:30,481 --> 00:02:33,481
My wool scarf, for the cold air-con on the train.

67
00:02:33,751 --> 00:02:35,531
I wrap up the whole box!

68
00:02:35,731 --> 00:02:37,221
But wool keeps you warm.

69
00:02:37,381 --> 00:02:39,161
Won't it warm up the ice cream?

70
00:02:39,513 --> 00:02:40,713
Let's find out.

71
00:02:40,973 --> 00:02:43,783
Be a tiny bit of air, trapped inside the wool!

72
00:02:44,063 --> 00:02:45,043
Shrink down.

73
00:02:45,323 --> 00:02:46,253
Quietly.

74
00:02:47,617 --> 00:02:50,807
You are a tiny bit of air, trapped between the curly wool

75
00:02:50,827 --> 00:02:51,717
fibres.

76
00:02:52,477 --> 00:02:54,627
They wrap around you like soft ropes.

77
00:02:54,838 --> 00:02:57,638
On one side is the hot afternoon air.

78
00:02:58,408 --> 00:03:01,068
On the other side is the frozen box.

79
00:03:01,278 --> 00:03:03,318
Heat flows in from the hot side.

80
00:03:04,068 --> 00:03:07,858
But heat does not flow easily through wool, or through trapped air

81
00:03:07,878 --> 00:03:08,678
like you.

82
00:03:08,878 --> 00:03:11,848
So the heat creeps in, very, very slowly.

83
00:03:13,481 --> 00:03:16,651
A poor conductor of heat is a material that heat does not

84
00:03:16,671 --> 00:03:21,051
flow through easily, such as wool, and the air trapped inside it.

85
00:03:21,647 --> 00:03:23,897
So wool does not make any heat at all?

86
00:03:24,221 --> 00:03:26,121
No, wool does not make heat.

87
00:03:26,391 --> 00:03:29,221
On a cold day, a scarf slows the heat flowing out of

88
00:03:29,241 --> 00:03:29,941
your neck.

89
00:03:30,211 --> 00:03:32,531
Today, it slows the heat flowing in.

90
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:36,149
Same scarf.

91
00:03:36,209 --> 00:03:37,859
It slows heat both ways.

92
00:03:38,211 --> 00:03:39,931
Okay, but I want proof!

93
00:03:40,061 --> 00:03:41,891
Then we do a fair test, like in Primary 3.

94
00:03:41,911 --> 00:03:44,741
The big box waits in the freezer.

95
00:03:44,943 --> 00:03:48,633
A fair test means we change only one thing, the wrapper, and

96
00:03:48,653 --> 00:03:50,343
keep everything else the same!

97
00:03:50,997 --> 00:03:53,977
Three cups of the same ice cream, in the same sun, for

98
00:03:53,997 --> 00:03:55,517
the same five minutes.

99
00:03:55,642 --> 00:03:59,302
Cup one gets no wrapper, cup two gets a thin plastic bag,

100
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,562
and cup three gets the wool scarf.

101
00:04:01,862 --> 00:04:03,862
Then we measure how much has melted.

102
00:04:04,065 --> 00:04:06,035
Which cup will have the least melted?

103
00:04:06,325 --> 00:04:07,475
Think about it.

104
00:04:12,256 --> 00:04:15,856
Five minutes later, the buddies pour out the melted part of each

105
00:04:15,876 --> 00:04:16,476
cup.

106
00:04:19,225 --> 00:04:21,205
The wool cup melted the least!

107
00:04:21,415 --> 00:04:23,175
Only five millilitres!

108
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:26,750
The thick wool, full of trapped air, slowed the heat flowing in

109
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,550
the most.

110
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:31,326
Okay, okay.

111
00:04:31,456 --> 00:04:33,086
The scarf is a hero.

112
00:04:33,366 --> 00:04:36,676
Now for the real rescue, under the covered walkway, out of the

113
00:04:36,696 --> 00:04:37,376
sun!

114
00:04:39,692 --> 00:04:40,512
Oh no!

115
00:04:40,712 --> 00:04:43,022
Our bottle opener fell into the drain!

116
00:04:43,114 --> 00:04:45,007
Don't worry, I've got a plan!

117
00:04:45,027 --> 00:04:46,287
No more plans, Pip.

118
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:47,737
I've got a magnet.

119
00:04:48,873 --> 00:04:52,473
The bottle opener is made of steel, and magnets attract iron and

120
00:04:52,493 --> 00:04:53,323
steel.

121
00:04:53,987 --> 00:04:56,687
My aluminium ring pull is still down there!

122
00:04:56,817 --> 00:04:59,257
Aluminium is not a magnetic material.

123
00:04:59,437 --> 00:05:00,697
Goodbye, ring pull.

124
00:05:01,047 --> 00:05:03,667
With one minute to spare, they open the box!

125
00:05:03,805 --> 00:05:05,485
It's still frozen hard!

126
00:05:05,575 --> 00:05:07,495
Snack emergency, solved!

127
00:05:08,426 --> 00:05:10,566
Who switched on the heat delivery service?

128
00:05:10,623 --> 00:05:12,683
Fan on us, not on the ice cream!

129
00:05:12,884 --> 00:05:15,134
Did you pick fix three, the wool scarf?

130
00:05:15,404 --> 00:05:17,764
Then you win a point, and so does Basil!

131
00:05:18,047 --> 00:05:20,447
Now, here are the words that earn marks.

132
00:05:20,504 --> 00:05:21,754
Say it with me!

133
00:05:22,465 --> 00:05:25,365
Heat flows from a hotter place to a colder place.

134
00:05:25,725 --> 00:05:27,955
Wool is a poor conductor of heat.

135
00:05:28,305 --> 00:05:31,675
It slows down the heat flowing from the warmer surroundings to the

136
00:05:31,695 --> 00:05:32,625
ice cream.

137
00:05:35,102 --> 00:05:36,022
What a year!

138
00:05:36,312 --> 00:05:41,622
In Primary 3, you sorted living things, tested materials, followed life cycles,

139
00:05:41,642 --> 00:05:42,922
and made magnets.

140
00:05:43,128 --> 00:05:44,498
And now, we level up.

141
00:05:47,422 --> 00:05:52,102
In Primary 4, get ready for systems, matter, light, shadows and heat!

142
00:05:52,249 --> 00:05:53,389
See you in Primary 4!

143
00:05:54,509 --> 00:05:56,709
Let's read today's key words together!

144
00:05:56,999 --> 00:05:57,759
Ready?

145
00:05:58,046 --> 00:05:59,326
Hotter to colder.

146
00:06:01,072 --> 00:06:02,642
Poor conductor of heat.

147
00:06:04,616 --> 00:06:05,636
Fair test.

148
00:06:07,067 --> 00:06:08,007
Well done!

149
00:06:08,989 --> 00:06:10,090
Say it with us!

150
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:11,640
Ready?

151
00:06:11,764 --> 00:06:12,424
One!

152
00:06:12,764 --> 00:06:13,464
two!

153
00:06:13,769 --> 00:06:14,944
Now you know!

154
00:06:20,154 --> 00:06:22,384
Wool is a poor conductor of meat!

155
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,120
Meat?

156
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,020
Did somebody say meat?
